  "description": "Front G1\tHolm Oak \t(Evergreen) x 2\t(Quercus ilex): trim 0.5m - 0.7m all round to shape. \tThese two oval shaped holm oak trees at the entrance to the building has not been maintained for two years. They have grown unruly and need tidying up.  There is an old nest at the top of one of the trees that has a lot of insects and bugs coming out of. Suggested work:- trim all round to make more compact oval shape\r- remove old nests\r\rMilford Lane\rT2\tGleditsia spp x 1\tThis 6m Gleditsia has grown at an angle over the footpath and now blocks the security camera. Suggested work:\r- crown reduction\r- reduce the height 2m\r- reduce the lateral growth 2-3m to balance crown\r- remove deadwood\rMilford Lane garden\rG3\tRiver Birch x 5 (Betula nigra)\t- lift over water feature to 2.5m- cut back off building to give 1m clearance \r- cut back off balconies to give 1.5m clearance\r- reduce height of end tree only so security",
